    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Junior Caminero** (73.35) headlining our offensive strategy. Both benefit significantly from a prime matchup against Imai and Kochanowicz, respectively, who possess xERAs of 5.17. **Christian Yelich** is the standout play, as his dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) and leadoff spot (+10%) create a high-floor environment for Runs and RBI. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** leverages a +19% SP skill boost to anchor the middle of the order. We are also capitalizing on speed-adjacent matchups; **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) is a strong start thanks to a favorable park, a +11% dynamic platoon edge, and a slow delivery from Gordon that enhances his stolen base potential. **Colt Keith** (63.27) rounds out our elite tier, utilizing his leadoff positioning to maximize efficiency against Burke.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on the bench, where **Chase Meidroth** (50.42) narrowly missed the final lineup spot. While his SP skill projection was solid at +13%, the optimizer favored the higher raw volume and platoon stability offered by the starters. We are monitoring the status of **Lars Nootbaar**, who remains on the IL, and **Hyeseong Kim**, currently developing in Oklahoma City. We must also exercise caution with **Trea Turner** (53.46) and **Kyle Schwarber** (54.85); while they are starting, both face the high-level arm of Yamamoto. Although wind conditions at the park provide a +5% boost, the sub-3.50 xERA of the opposing pitcher necessitates careful monitoring of their plate appearances. We continue to hold **Zac Veen**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** in reserve as we maintain our focus on daily efficiency and maximizing stolen base opportunities.",
